OpenCode is an AI coding agent for the terminal. This companion port installs
the opencode_serve rc.d boot service that runs `opencode serve` as an
unprivileged user, so the OpenCode Desktop app and `opencode attach` clients
can connect to a persistent remote server.

It sources an env file for secrets (provider API keys and an HTTP basic auth
password), listens on 127.0.0.1:4555 by default for SSH-tunnel access, and
preserves persistent terminals across service restarts through a PTY handoff.

The opencode binary itself is installed by misc/opencode.
